@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Charts/Overview")]

<h1>Charts</h1>

<h2><code>ChartLegend</code></h2>
<p>A row of entries that names what a chart's colours and shapes mean; it wraps to more rows when it is too narrow. Each <code>LegendItem</code> has a swatch, a label and an optional <code>Marker</code> glyph such as ▲, so colour is not the only cue. With no items nothing is rendered.</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Swatch</th><th>Looks like</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Accent</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-accent</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Chip</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-chip</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Error</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-error</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Outline</td><td>A dashed ring in <code>--color-border-strong</code>, for something absent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Line</td><td>A short dashed line in <code>--color-text-muted</code>, for a reference line.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Band</td><td>An unfilled box, twice as wide as tall, edged in <code>--color-chart-band</code>, for a target band. Apps stroke the band's top and bottom edges in this colour with no fill.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<ul>
    <li>The list is labelled "Legend"; the swatches are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>{TestId}-0</code>, <code>{TestId}-1</code>, … by position.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>ProgressRing</code></h2>
<p>A ring that fills as <code>Value</code> approaches <code>Max</code>, with the value in the middle. Above <code>Max</code> it turns <code>--color-error</code> and the number does too. <code>Compact</code> uses the smaller <code>--ring-size-compact</code>. The ring is meant to sit on a card (<code>--color-surface</code>); its track is tuned for that surface.</p>
<ul>
    <li>With a zero or negative <code>Max</code> there is no maximum: the ring is full once <code>Value</code> is above zero, and never over.</li>
    <li><code>Caption</code> is a short line under the number; <code>ChildContent</code> replaces the number, for a figure such as what is left, in which case set <code>AriaLabel</code> to describe it.</li>
    <li>The ring is an image named by <code>AriaLabel</code>, by default "{value} of {max} {caption}"; its centre is hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>{TestId}-value</code> and <code>{TestId}-caption</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>BarList</code></h2>
<p>Labelled horizontal bars, one per <code>BarListItem</code>, each with its value text at the end of the row. Bars are sized against the largest value, or against <code>Max</code> when it is a positive number. Negative and non-finite values fill no bar; the default value text shows a negative number as it is and a non-finite one as 0. Like <code>ProgressRing</code>, it is meant to sit on a card (<code>--color-surface</code>): the track keeps 3:1 against that surface, not against the page.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>ValueText</code> replaces the value shown, by default the number with thousands separators and no decimals. A long label is cut with an ellipsis.</li>
    <li>With no items <code>EmptyText</code> is shown instead of the list.</li>
    <li>The list is named by <code>Label</code>; the bars are hidden from screen readers, so put what matters in the label and value text.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>{TestId}-row-0</code>, <code>-label-0</code>, <code>-value-0</code> and <code>-bar-0</code> by position, or <code>{TestId}-empty</code> with no items. None are rendered without <code>TestId</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>TrendBarChart</code></h2>
<p>A bar chart of one value per slot, such as a week of days or a year of months, judged against a <code>Target</code>. Bars are <code>TrendBar</code> records; a bar with no value leaves an empty slot. The chart is meant to sit on a card (<code>--color-surface</code>).</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Looks like</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Under</td><td>A bar in <code>--color-chip</code>, more than 10% below the target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>On target</td><td>A bar in <code>--color-accent</code>, within 10% either side of the target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Over</td><td>A bar in <code>--color-error</code> with a ▲ marker above it, more than 10% over.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Target</td><td>A dashed line (<code>--chart-dash</code>) at the target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Target range</td><td>The band 10% either side of the target, drawn as a top and bottom edge in <code>--color-chart-band</code> at <code>--border-width</code> with no fill, so no bar loses contrast.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<ul>
    <li>Without a target (or with zero) there is no line, no band and no status.</li>
    <li>With <code>OnSelect</code> the bars are buttons: click, or Enter on focus, raises it with the bar's date. Without it they are images.</li>
    <li>Each bar's text alternative is its date, value, <code>Unit</code>, status and <code>Note</code>; a bar with a <code>Note</code> is drawn faded. The chart is a group named by <code>Label</code>; with no values it shows <code>EmptyText</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>-band</code> (<code>-band-top</code>, <code>-band-bottom</code>), <code>-target</code>, <code>-baseline</code>, <code>-tick-{value}</code>, <code>-bar-{date}</code>, <code>-column-{date}</code>, <code>-marker-{date}</code>, <code>-gap-{date}</code>, <code>-value-label</code>, <code>-empty</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>MonthCalendar</code></h2>
<p>A grid of one month, Monday first unless <code>FirstDayOfWeek</code> says otherwise, with a cell per day judged against a <code>Target</code>. Days are <code>CalendarDay</code> records; a day missing from <code>Days</code>, or without a value, counts as not recorded. It is meant to sit on a card (<code>--color-surface</code>).</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>Looks like</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Under</td><td>A cell in <code>--color-chip</code>, more than 10% below the target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>On target</td><td>A cell in <code>--color-accent</code>, within 10% either side of the target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Over</td><td>A cell in <code>--color-error</code> with a ▲ marker, more than 10% over.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Not recorded</td><td>A dashed outline in <code>--color-border-strong</code> and no fill.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Future</td><td>Faded and disabled; data on a future day is ignored.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Today</td><td>A <code>--color-text</code> ring and bold number. <code>Today</code> sets the day; without it the clock does.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<ul>
    <li>Without a target (or with zero) a recorded day has no status, unless the day carries its own target.</li>
    <li><code>FirstDayOfWeek</code> (Monday by default) sets the first column. <code>DayNames</code> is seven labels, Sunday first; without it each heading is the first letter of the current culture's shortest day name, and a list of any other length throws.</li>
    <li>With <code>OnSelect</code> the enabled days are buttons that raise it with the day's date; without it they are plain cells.</li>
    <li>Each day's text alternative is its date, "today" when it is, its value, <code>Unit</code> and status, or "not recorded" or "future". The grid is a group named by the month; the weekday letters are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>-day-{date}</code> and <code>-marker-{date}</code>, the date as yyyy-MM-dd.</li>
</ul>

